G83 takes an optional I word: the feed rate for the move from R back down
into the hole, to D above the bottom of the previous peck. Without I that
move is a rapid, as before.

Covers: no I (rapids, unchanged); I (the move back in is a feed at I and F is
restored for the next peck); I with a D past R (nothing to feed, the clamp to
R still applies, so no zero-length move); I read per block, not carried to
the next line; an earlier G87 I not leaking into G83; the G18 plane; and the
refused cases (I <= 0, also on a modal line; I on G81). G83 on the same line
as G68.2 or G68.4, which also read I, is already refused because both use
axis words; the test pins that down too.
